---
# Rename to migrations.md (drop .example) to activate. Loads only when Claude reads/edits a matching file.
paths:
  - "packages/db/migrations/**"
  - "packages/db/src/**"
---

# Database migrations

- Migrations are forward-only, numbered SQL files. Never edit a merged migration; add a new one.
- Expand-only: every migration must work with the previous release's code (rollback is app-only).
- Claim the next number in the migrations README ledger in the same PR.
- Never run migrations against production. That is Rich's step (ask first).
- Any PR touching this path is lane 3 (also listed in HARD_PATHS in .github/workflows/lane.yml): Rich adds merge-ok and merges.
- Reviewer checklist: locks on large tables, NOT NULL without default, data backfills, destructive DROP/RENAME.
